\fs32\b Uploading\b0\fs20\par
\par
When the transcription is complete and every row has been verified, it can be uploaded to FreeBMD.\par
\par
\fs24\b Before uploading\b0\fs20\par
Make sure that all entries on the scan have been transcribed and verified.\par
\par
A tick mark should appear at the end of every verified row in the transcription grid.\par
\par
WinBMD2 will not allow a normal upload to proceed while required checks are still outstanding.\par
\par
\fs24\b Starting the upload\b0\fs20\par
Click Upload above the transcription grid.\par
\par
WinBMD2 checks the transcription before sending it to FreeBMD. If a problem is found which prevents the upload, a message will explain what needs attention.\par
\par
\fs24\b FreeBMD User ID and password\b0\fs20\par
The upload is made using the Current FreeBMD User ID and Password shown on the Header Form.\par
\par
These identify the person currently submitting the transcription to FreeBMD.\par
\par
If these details need to be changed, use Edit Header before uploading.\par
\par
\fs24\b Uploading the transcription\b0\fs20\par
When the checks have been completed successfully, WinBMD2 sends the transcription to FreeBMD.\par
\par
Wait for WinBMD2 to report the result of the upload before closing the program or making further changes to the transcription.\par
\par
\fs24\b If the upload is unsuccessful\b0\fs20\par
If FreeBMD does not accept the upload, WinBMD2 will display information about the problem.\par
\par
Correct anything which needs attention and try the upload again.\par
\par
Do not assume that the transcription has been received by FreeBMD unless WinBMD2 reports that the upload was successful.\par
